<abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>Synchronization information represents the difference ( beta ) between the PCR value E and the count N (=3,240,000), assuming that the third PCR packet arrives at a transmitter (201) at the time (time t1) when the count N turns 3,240,000 from the difference ( alpha ) between the PCR value E3 and the count N3 occurring while clocks corresponding to the difference (count N3-reference clock B) are counted. Hence delay fluctuation occurring on a network is eliminated.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Des informations de synchronisation représentent la différence ( beta ) entre la valeur référence temporelle de programme (PCR) E et le chiffre N (égal à 3 240 000), si l'on suppose que le troisième paquet PCR arrive au niveau d'un émetteur (201) au moment (moment t1) où le chiffre N atteint 3 240 000. On obtient la différence ( alpha ) entre la valeur PCR E3 et le chiffre N3 en comptant les horloges qui correspondent à la différence (chiffre N3-horloge de référence B). On élimine ainsi toute variation dans les retards pouvant se produire sur un réseau.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>